{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-11-13T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Just north of Moab, Utah, Arches National Park is home to more than 2,000 natural sandstone arches – the densest concentration of arches in the world. Today's image, North Window, is one of the best-known formations in the park's Windows Section, where towering fins, openings and sculpted sandstone create a landscape that looks almost architectural.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_EN-CA6553146914_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_EN-CA6553146914_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Architecture without an architect","Title":"North Window, Arches National Park, Moab, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© lightphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/38.6857117,-109.5328291/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=38.6857117,-109.5328291;S9;North Window, Arches National Park, Moab, Utah&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Arches+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261112_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow"},"Ssd":"20261112","Name":"NorthWindow","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6553146914","FullDateString":"Nov 12, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Atlantic Forest is one of the world's great biodiversity hotspots, stretching along much of Brazil's Atlantic coast and into Argentina and Paraguay. Its landscape includes tropical and subtropical forests, mangroves and coastal habitats, providing a home for around 20,000 plant species and an extraordinary variety of wildlife, including jaguars and golden lion tamarins. Much of the forest has disappeared over the centuries, but it continues to play an important role in storing carbon and providing fresh water for millions of people across the region.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_EN-CA7496830701_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_EN-CA7496830701_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A forest full of wonder","Title":"The Atlantic Forest, Brazil","Copyright":"© FG Trade/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The Atlantic Forest is home to around 150 million people, which is roughly a third of South America's total population.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Atlantic+Forest+Brazil&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261111_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica"},"Ssd":"20261111","Name":"Atlantica","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"7496830701","FullDateString":"Nov 11, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Rose Island is a picture-perfect escape in The Bahamas, where lush greenery meets some of the most vibrant blue waters in the Caribbean. Located just a short boat ride from Nassau, this peaceful cay is known for its pristine beaches, crystal-clear shallows and relaxed island atmosphere. Movie fans may recognize it as a filming location from the 1965 James Bond adventure Thunderball, but today Rose Island's biggest attractions are its natural beauty and unique wildlife, including its famous swimming pigs. Viewed from above, the island showcases the dazzling colours that make The Bahamas world-renowned, with turquoise lagoons, sandy shoals and clear waters creating a breathtaking tropical landscape.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_EN-CA5604124548_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_EN-CA5604124548_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Licensed to chill","Title":"Aerial view of Rose Island, The Bahamas","Copyright":"© Abstract Aerial Art/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/25.088243,-77.225304/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=25.088243,-77.225304;S9;Rose Island, The Bahamas&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rose+Island+Bahamas&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261110_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland"},"Ssd":"20261110","Name":"RoseIsland","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"5604124548","FullDateString":"Nov 10, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Cross the Guadalquivir River and discover Triana, one of Seville’s most vibrant neighbourhoods. Connected to the city’s historic centre by the iconic Triana Bridge since the 19th century, this riverside district is known for its colourful ceramics, flamenco heritage and lively local culture. Brightly decorated buildings, traditional tile workshops and bustling markets give Triana a character all its own. Stroll along Calle Betis for scenic river views, explore streets lined with artisan studios, or simply soak up the neighbourhood’s welcoming atmosphere. While Seville’s famous landmarks are just steps away, Triana offers a unique glimpse into the traditions, creativity and everyday life that help define Andalusia.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_EN-CA5715664258_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_EN-CA5715664258_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where art finds its rhythm","Title":"Historic district of Triana, Seville, Spain","Copyright":"© Andrzej Rostek/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.382904,-6.006341/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.382904,-6.006341;S9;Triana, Seville, Spain&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Seville+Spain&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261109_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain"},"Ssd":"20261109","Name":"TrianaSpain","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"5715664258","FullDateString":"Nov 9, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Diwali, the Festival of Lights, is celebrated by millions of people around the world, including vibrant communities across Canada. Rooted in the Sanskrit word dipavali, meaning “row of lights,” the festival symbolizes the triumph of light over darkness and hope over adversity. Families and friends gather to light diyas and lanterns, create colourful rangoli, share sweets and take part in prayers and celebrations. While traditions vary across regions and faiths, Diwali is widely recognized as a time of reflection, gratitude and togetherness. As communities across Canada come together to celebrate, the festival continues to brighten neighbourhoods, workplaces and schools with its message of unity, joy and renewal.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DiwaliLamps_EN-CA5815375040_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DiwaliLamps_EN-CA5815375040_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A celebration that shines","Title":"Lanterns for Diwali, Mumbai, Maharashtra, India","Copyright":"© Dinodia Photo/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/18.969048,72.821182/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=18.969048,72.821182;S9;Mumbai, Maharashtra, India&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261108_DiwaliLamps\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Diwali&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261108_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261108_DiwaliLamps"},"Ssd":"20261108","Name":"DiwaliLamps","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"5815375040","FullDateString":"Nov 8, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"One of North America's most remarkable animals, the bison is a powerful symbol of strength, resilience and conservation. Weighing as much as 900 kilograms (2,000 pounds) and capable of running up to 55 km/h (35 mph), bison are surprisingly agile. Despite being commonly called buffalo, American bison are a distinct species known for their massive shoulder hump, curved horns and shaggy coats that help them thrive through harsh winters. Once pushed to the brink of extinction, bison have made an inspiring comeback thanks to conservation efforts across Canada and the United States, making them a powerful example of successful wildlife recovery.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_EN-CA6055061732_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_EN-CA6055061732_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The giant that came back","Title":"A bison in the grasslands of Theodore Roosevelt National Park, North Dakota, USA","Copyright":"© Tandem Stock/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/47.275714,-103.463282/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=47.275714,-103.463282;S9;Theodore Roosevelt National Park, North Dakota&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261107_DakotaBison\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Bison&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261107_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261107_DakotaBison"},"Ssd":"20261107","Name":"DakotaBison","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6055061732","FullDateString":"Nov 7, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Haleakalā National Park on Maui is home to an extraordinary mix of landscapes, from volcanic slopes and rainforest to towering bamboo forests. The park stretches from the summit of Haleakalā, which rises 3,055 metres above sea level, to the Pacific coast. More than 850 plant species grow here, including some found nowhere else on Earth, alongside native Hawaiian wildlife. One of the park's most popular walks is the Pīpīwai Trail, which winds through lush forest before reaching a remarkable bamboo grove. As the bamboo sways in the breeze, its tall stalks create distinctive sounds that add to the unique experience.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_EN-CA6167003961_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_EN-CA6167003961_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A green tunnel through Maui","Title":"Bamboo forest, Pīpīwai Trail, Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii, USA","Copyright":"© MNStudio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/20.760987,-156.155095/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=20.760987,-156.155095;S9;Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Haleakala+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261106_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail"},"Ssd":"20261106","Name":"PipiwaiTrail","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6167003961","FullDateString":"Nov 6, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"It's World Philosophy Day, when big thinkers gather to discuss life's eternal mysteries. To celebrate, today's image features the \"Body of Knowledge\" sculpture at Goethe University in Frankfurt, Germany, which molds steel letters from eight different alphabets into a human form. Spanish artist Jaume Plensa explains: \"Our body is the home of the spirit. The place in which ideas live.\" On World Philosophy Day, we're all encouraged to look beyond easy answers and explore the questions that shape us, and the world around us.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KnowledgeSculpture_EN-CA4919138764_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KnowledgeSculpture_EN-CA4919138764_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Where ideas take shape","Title":"The \"Body of Knowledge\" sculpture by Jaume Plensa at Goethe University in Frankfurt, Germany","Copyright":"© Todamo/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.127805,8.667807/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.127805,8.667807;S9;Goethe University, Frankfurt&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261119_KnowledgeSculpture\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Philosophy+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261119_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261119_KnowledgeSculpture"},"Ssd":"20261119","Name":"KnowledgeSculpture","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"4919138764","FullDateString":"Nov 19, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"These barn owls, bathed in evening light, are waiting for the hunt to begin. As night falls, these birds of prey swoop into action, listening for tiny movements in grass or leaves made by mice and voles. Their heart-shaped faces help funnel sound into some of the sharpest ears in the animal kingdom. This allows them to locate their prey with pinpoint precision in the dark before swooping silently, their soft feathers muffling their approach. In fall, young barn owls strike out to find their own territories. As the nights grow longer, you might spot them earlier in the evening, gliding over fields in search of dinner.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BarnOwlsUnite_EN-CA4667422481_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BarnOwlsUnite_EN-CA4667422481_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Hunting from dusk till dawn","Title":"Pair of barn owls","Copyright":"© Zahoor Salmi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Barn owls don't hoot; they make eerie, screeching noises, which might explain their reputation as harbingers of doom.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261118_BarnOwlsUnite\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Barn+owl&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261118_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261118_BarnOwlsUnite"},"Ssd":"20261118","Name":"BarnOwlsUnite","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"4667422481","FullDateString":"Nov 18, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"It's time to breathe in that crisp fall air and step into the great outdoors. Today's image features the Trail of the Cedars, part of more than 1,100 kilometres of hiking trails in Glacier National Park, Montana. Its 1.4-kilometre loop includes a raised boardwalk which cuts a path through western red cedars and hemlock trees. The park boasts routes for all abilities, taking in alpine lakes, wildflower meadows, mountain passes and wilderness stretching to the Canadian border. But if you don't have spectacular scenery on your doorstep, a short stroll along a tree-lined street is an easy way to celebrate and enjoy the benefits of getting out, as the days draw in.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TrailCedars_EN-CA4398712905_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TrailCedars_EN-CA4398712905_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Step into the great outdoors","Title":"Trail of the Cedars, Glacier National Park, Montana, USA","Copyright":"© DBushue Photography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.706957,-113.817235/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.706957,-113.817235;S9;Glacier National Park, Montana&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261117_TrailCedars\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Trail+of+the+Cedars%2c+Glacier+National+Park%2c+Montana&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261117_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261117_TrailCedars"},"Ssd":"20261117","Name":"TrailCedars","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"4398712905","FullDateString":"Nov 17, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Incredible views and rock-solid foundations are part of the charm of these ancient dwellings, set into the cliffside in New Mexico. Nomads had long used the natural caves above Cliff Dweller Creek as temporary shelter, but it was the Native American Mogollon people who made them their home. Archaeologists believe they created dozens of rooms inside five alcoves in the 1270s and 1280s. Up to 15 families lived here at any one time, raising children, making pottery and overlooking the fertile Gila River valley where they grew crops and hunted wildlife. For reasons unknown, the Mogollon people moved on around 1300, leaving behind one of the American Southwest's most important archaeological sites.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GilaCliff_EN-CA4135486351_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GilaCliff_EN-CA4135486351_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Built to last","Title":"Gila Cliff Dwellings National Monument, New Mexico, USA","Copyright":"© Chiara Salvadori/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/33.254028,-108.272634/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=33.254028,-108.272634;S9;Gila Cliff Dwellings National Monument, New Mexico&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261116_GilaCliff\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Gila+Cliff+Dwellings+National+Monument&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261116_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261116_GilaCliff"},"Ssd":"20261116","Name":"GilaCliff","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"4135486351","FullDateString":"Nov 16, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As fall's first frost sets in, ice crystals form on the leaves of evergreen shrubs, like this azalea. Long gone are the pinks, oranges and yellows of their spring blooms, but a new colourful display awaits, as their green leaves turn shades of red and purple. For the plants, the new pigments protect their leaves as temperatures drop, but for gardeners, they create a vibrant fall display, framed in white frost. When spring arrives, new growth will restore the shrub's green leaves, and the colourful cycle begins anew.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FirstFrost_EN-CA3834515702_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FirstFrost_EN-CA3834515702_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Frosty foliage","Title":"Frozen azalea with red leaves","Copyright":"© avoferten/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The pigments that turn azalea leaves shades of red or purple are called anthocyanins.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261115_FirstFrost\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=azaleas&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261115_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261115_FirstFrost"},"Ssd":"20261115","Name":"FirstFrost","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"3834515702","FullDateString":"Nov 15, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Welcome to Hong Kong, home to the world's largest collection of skyscrapers. Those pictured here tower above Victoria Harbour, whose deep waters allowed the island to develop as a busy trading port. Ships carrying tea, silk and other goods have passed through since the 1840s, but growth rocketed in the decades after World War II, fuelling a construction boom. With little flat land available between the harbour and the hills, developers had to build upward, creating this distinctive skyline. In 2026, Hong Kong has 569 completed buildings at least 150 metres tall — more than any other city.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BlueHK_EN-CA2709774125_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BlueHK_EN-CA2709774125_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The only way is up","Title":"Victoria Harbour, Hong Kong, China","Copyright":"© Juan Romero/Cavan Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/22.285,114.165/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=22.285,114.165;S9;Victoria Harbour, Hong Kong&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261114_BlueHK\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Victoria+Harbour+Hong+Kong&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261114_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261114_BlueHK"},"Ssd":"20261114","Name":"BlueHK","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"2709774125","FullDateString":"Nov 14, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Dawn's first light is reflected on the frozen surface of Abraham Lake, framed by Rocky Mountains peaks. In winter, this picturesque lake in Alberta is famous for its frozen bubbles of methane gas, trapped beneath the ice. Strong winds keep the surface clear of snow, offering winter-long views. Come spring, when the ice thaws, the gas escapes into the atmosphere.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AbrahamCanada_EN-CA3327574008_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AbrahamCanada_EN-CA3327574008_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Hidden depths","Title":"Abraham Lake in Alberta","Copyright":"© Guang Cao/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/52.1392,-116.4355/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=52.1392,-116.4355;S9;Abraham Lake, Alberta&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=3